    "In the same private successor module stage ReleaseArtifactSlot, ReleaseArtifactManifest and entries plus intent digest construction as pure domain additions; do not replace exported ArtifactSlotId/ArtifactManifestV1 or accept a second production document until PM-004/005's joint cutover.",
    "Encode the sole supported product targets in typed model authority: aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, aarch64-unknown-linux-musl, and wasm32-wasip1; reject all other, duplicate, unsafe, omitted, or extra product slots.",
    "Add typed immutable provenance policy to every slot and include every policy field in the intent digest.",
    "Implement canonical ReleaseDistributionMetadataV1 construction from the immutable intent plus validated product payload entries, with strict serialization/schema checks and no independently supplied payload roster.",
    "Implement checksum-roster validation: payloads and final metadata appear once, checksum itself is excluded from its own digest list, and the final manifest includes checksum and metadata slots.",
    "Require manifest validation to cover every declared registry/product/checksum/metadata slot exactly once with exact source, digest, length, target, filename, and policy bindings.",
    "Add model tests for all four-target positive roster; each missing/extra/duplicate/wrong-target/unsafe slot; byte/source/slot substitutions; malformed provenance; metadata canonicalization; checksum circularity avoidance; and no compatibility decoder.",
    "Run rtk just test; expected: all successor artifact and metadata tests pass.",
    "Run rtk just fmt-check and rtk just lint; expected: both exit zero.",
    "CUTOVER-1 promotes this exact implementation, removes the staging module boundary and old V1 shapes, and migrates every immediate consumer. No implementation of graph observer, provider dispatch, ReleaseObservationEvidence or receipt construction belongs to PM-001/002."
  ],
  "commit_message": "feat(model): add release artifact inventory and metadata",
  "depends_on": [
    "PM-001"
  ],
  "covers_criteria": [
    "AC-004",
    "AC-006",
    "AC-007",
    "AC-010",
    "AC-011"
  ]
}

